# Section background alternation rule

Every full-bleed section rendered directly in a page's `<main>` (excluding
hero sections, which keep their own bespoke background and sit above this
sequence) is either:

- **Purple** — `bg-(--surface)` on the section's root `<section>`
  (`var(--surface)` = `#F4EFFF`, already global in `app/globals.css`, no new
  token needed).
- **White** (default) — no override class, inherits the page background.

Reading down the page, consecutive sections must alternate purple/white —
never two of the same back to back — with two allowed deliberate exceptions:
a logo-strip section right after the hero stays white (tinted backgrounds
read poorly behind a logo marquee), and any section whose own inner markup
already renders a card/panel at `var(--surface)` (or an equivalent tint like
`--violet-tint`) must stay white at the section level, or that inner
card/panel visually disappears into the section background.

When a section is purple, cards/content boxes on top of it stay white
(`background:#fff; border:1px solid var(--border)`) — never colored cards
(established pattern: `.chal-card`, `.cap-card`, `.mach-card`, `.who-card`).

**Implementation:** every section component takes an optional `purple`
boolean prop, default `false`. `false`/omitted → no class added, zero visual
change. `true` → adds `bg-(--surface)` to the section's className. Shared
cross-page components (`FaqSection`, `FinalCTA`) must default `purple` to
`false` so other pages calling them unprompted are unaffected.

Before wiring a new section, check it doesn't already have a plain
(non-Tailwind) CSS `background` rule — unlayered CSS always beats Tailwind's
`@layer utilities`, so `bg-(--surface)` would silently no-op. If one exists
(e.g. `FinalCTA`'s `.final-card-section { background:#fff }`), use an inline
`style={{ background: "var(--surface)" }}` instead, which always wins.

Full rationale, exact background/token values, and the exception list live
in `AGENTS.md` under "Section background alternation rule (sitewide)" — that
is the canonical source. If the rule changes, update AGENTS.md first and
mirror the bullets above.
